{
  "tema": 5132,
  "slug": "se-impersonal",
  "titulo": "Impersonal se = one, you, people",
  "subtitulo": "Aquí se come bien.",
  "foto": "t03.jpg",
  "regla": "To talk about people in general (English _one_, _you_, _people_) or to give instructions, use **se** + the verb in the 3rd person singular: aquí se come bien, ¿cómo se dice…? If a plural noun follows, the verb goes plural: se venden casas.",
  "comparada_kwiziq": null,
  "secciones": [
    {
      "id": "regla",
      "titulo": "The rule",
      "bloques": [
        {
          "tipo": "texto",
          "texto": "English often uses a general _you_, _one_ or _people_: _You eat well here_. Spanish uses **se** + the verb in the **él / ella** form."
        },
        {
          "tipo": "formula",
          "partes": [
            "se",
            "+",
            "verb in the 3rd person singular"
          ]
        },
        {
          "tipo": "texto",
          "texto": "No one in particular is named: **se** stands for anyone."
        },
        {
          "tipo": "texto",
          "texto": "It's perfect for **instructions** and **recipes**: **Se pica** la cebolla y **se fríe** en aceite."
        },
        {
          "tipo": "texto",
          "texto": "If a **plural** noun follows the verb, the verb goes **plural**: **se venden** tacos, **se rentan** tablas. (That's the passive se.)"
        },
        {
          "tipo": "texto",
          "texto": "A general **tú** is also heard (**aquí comes bien**), but for rules, signs and instructions **se** is the norm: **No se puede fumar aquí.**"
        },
        {
          "tipo": "texto",
          "texto": "Tip: **se** is the faceless crowd: nobody in particular, everybody in general."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "ejemplos",
      "titulo": "Examples",
      "bloques": [
        {
          "tipo": "ejemplos",
          "lista": [
            {
              "es": "Aquí ==se come== muy bien.",
              "en": "You eat really well here."
            },
            {
              "es": "¿Cómo ==se dice== _wave_ en español?",
              "en": "How do you say \"wave\" in Spanish?"
            },
            {
              "es": "En el gimnasio no ==se entra== con zapatos.",
              "en": "You don't go into the gym with shoes on."
            },
            {
              "es": "Primero ==se lava== el arroz y luego ==se fríe== un poco.",
              "en": "First you wash the rice and then you fry it a little."
            },
            {
              "es": "Por esta calle ==se llega== a la playa.",
              "en": "You get to the beach along this street."
            },
            {
              "es": "No ==se puede== estacionar aquí.",
              "en": "You can't park here."
            },
            {
              "es": "En Tijuana ==se vive== bien.",
              "en": "People live well in Tijuana."
            },
            {
              "es": "==Se venden== plantas de jitomate.",
              "en": "Tomato plants for sale."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "trampa",
      "titulo": "The trap",
      "bloques": [
        {
          "tipo": "pares",
          "lista": [
            {
              "filas": [
                {
                  "v": "mal",
                  "t": "¿Cómo dice _wave_ en español?"
                },
                {
                  "v": "bien",
                  "t": "¿Cómo se dice _wave_ en español?"
                }
              ],
              "nota": "Without **se** it means _how does he / she say_."
            },
            {
              "filas": [
                {
                  "v": "mal",
                  "t": "Aquí se comen bien."
                },
                {
                  "v": "bien",
                  "t": "Aquí se come bien."
                }
              ],
              "nota": "No plural noun: singular verb."
            },
            {
              "filas": [
                {
                  "v": "mal",
                  "t": "Se vende tablas de surf."
                },
                {
                  "v": "bien",
                  "t": "Se venden tablas de surf."
                }
              ],
              "nota": "Plural noun: plural verb."
            },
            {
              "filas": [
                {
                  "v": "mal",
                  "t": "No se puedes fumar aquí."
                },
                {
                  "v": "bien",
                  "t": "No se puede fumar aquí."
                }
              ],
              "nota": "**Se** takes the él / ella form, never the tú form."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
